        "name": "Nelson Romaine"
      },
      "message": "Switch to cookie-only auth delegation (no per-app JWT mint)\n\nReplaces the mint-and-store-JWT pattern with cookie-only delegation.\nauth.romaine.life owns the session via a .romaine.life-scoped cookie that\nthe browser auto-attaches on every request to workout.romaine.life.\nBackend forwards the cookie to auth.romaine.life's get-session endpoint\non each request (cached 60s) and gates on the returned role claim.\n\nReasoning\n---------\nTank-operator mints + stores a session JWT because it bundles per-user\nprofile data (github_login, installation_id, run_prefs) into the token,\nmaking every read self-contained. Kill-me has no equivalent — it just\nre-signed the same {sub, email, name, role} that auth.romaine.life\nalready issued. That extra mint added per-app KV secret + role\nassignments + a localStorage token, none of which paid for themselves.\n\nPer tank-operator/docs/quality-timeframes.md \"the durable data model or\nstate ownership is explicit\" and \"local UI state that can contradict\ndurable state\" — auth.romaine.life is the durable owner; the localStorage\nJWT was shadow state with TTL drift.\n\nThis also resolves the prod-503 state: pod no longer reads\nkill-me-jwt-signing-secret, so the workload-identity-scope-on-renamed-\nsecret problem (blocked by the kill-me tfstate lock) is moot.\n\nEnd-to-end deletions\n--------------------\n- backend/auth-routes.js (no /api/auth/exchange, no /api/auth/logout)\n- backend/auth.js HS256 verifier + jose-based JWKS verifier; replaced\n  with a cookie-forward middleware\n- backend/config.js KV secret read (cosmos_db_endpoint is the only thing\n  left to fetch)\n- backend/package.json: dropped jose + jsonwebtoken\n- frontend/src/auth/index.js: dropped fetchUpstreamJWT, exchange(),\n  getStoredToken, clearStoredToken, all localStorage handling\n- frontend/src/auth/AuthContext.jsx: dropped token state, just user/loading\n- frontend/src/api/client.js: dropped Authorization header; uses\n  credentials: 'include' so the .romaine.life cookie auto-attaches\n- frontend/src/api/snapshotContext.jsx: switched from `token` to `user`\n  for live/snapshot routing\n- tofu/keyvault.tf (entire file — no per-app signing secret)\n- tofu/identity.tf: dropped azurerm_role_assignment.kill_me_kv_jwt_secret\n- k8s/templates/serviceaccount.yaml comment updated\n\nGuard\n-----\nscripts/check-removed-msal.mjs extended to block reintroduction of\njsonwebtoken, jose, jwt.sign/verify, createRemoteJWKSet,\n/api/auth/exchange, localStorage 'token', and kill-me-jwt-signing-secret.\n\nTofu apply on merge will destroy the now-unused KV secret and the\nrole assignment. (Whether the kill-me state lock from prior runs has\nexpired remains to be seen — if apply fails on lock, force-unlock\nneeded once.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
